  }
  function editableAt(x, y) {
    /* PASS 631b - MEASURED, AND THE REASON NOTHING HAPPENED ON A STICKY NOTE.
       A note is opened inside a panel that lays a full-screen backdrop over
       the page, so elementFromPoint answered `sticky-panel-back` and the
       writable body of the note underneath was never seen. A pen wrote anyway,
       because a pen writes anywhere, which is why the pen case passed its test
       and the finger case failed hers.

       Three ways of asking, in order of trust:
         1. the whole stack under the point, not just its top;
         2. failing that, geometry: the smallest writable box that contains the
            point, which no overlay can hide;
         3. failing that, nothing, and the caller falls back to the caret. */
